# Paranal Airglow Line And Continuum Emission (PALACE) model: data and code of
# v1.0 (Noll et al. 2024)
# 
# OH level populations from measured reference intensities of Lambda doublets
# (based on X-shooter/UVES data) that were used for the OH population model
# 
# Column names:
# lam: central vacuum wavelength in µm (HITRAN2020)
# dlam: distance of Lambda doublet components from lam in µm
# ID: 12 characters describing upper and lower states (HITRAN2020)
#     (see pmd_reflineint_mol.dat for details)
# vi: vibrational level of upper state
# Fi: electronic substate of upper state (1 or 2)
# Ni: rotational level of upper state
# Ei: energy of upper state in 1/cm (HITRAN2020)
# Aij: Einstein-A coefficient in 1/s (HITRAN2020)
# Aijc: corrected Einstein-A coefficient in 1/s (see pmd_corrA_Ohbands.dat
#       for branch and band corrections)
# gi: statistical weight (HITRAN2020)
# I: measured reference intensity in R
# src: source of I: x = X-shooter-based climatology (partly from noll+23),
#      u = UVES mean spectrum (noll+20), c = UVES mean spectrum (cosby+06)
# y: natural logarithm of population in Rs, i.e. ln(I/(Aijc*gi))
# 
# References:
# cosby+06: https://doi.org/10.1029/2006JA012023 (only vi = 10)
# HITRAN2020: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jqsrt.2021.107949
# noll+20: https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-20-5269-2020 (< 1.05 µm)
# noll+23: https://doi.org/10.1029/2022JD038275 (> 1.005 µm)
# 
